tutor.text:
Here’s the loop with the right condition and a tiny tweak: 

```js
while (lo <= hi) {
  const mid = Math.floor((lo + hi) / 2);
  if (nums[mid] < target) lo = mid + 1;
  else hi = mid - 1;
}
``` 

Now lo moves past mid when the middle value is too small, and hi moves before mid when it’s too big. That prevents the pointers from getting stuck on the same index. Give it a try—what should the final return check look like now?

